Description: Provides a modular and extensible framework for designing and
    executing algorithmic workflows from interchangeable engine components
    for data splitting, execution, preprocessing, training, in-processing,
    post-processing, evaluation, reporting and publishing. Each engine
    category has a standardized input and output interface, and controller
    functions validate inputs and manage execution, which supports
    systematic reuse, benchmarking and transparent, reproducible analyses.
    A core application is fairness-aware modeling, with ready-to-use
    engines for fairness interventions before, during and after model
    training. Workflows run sequentially or in parallel via 'batchtools'
    (locally or on 'SLURM' clusters), can stop adaptively once results are
    stable, and can be resumed after interruption. The framework is
    described in Willer and Ruckdeschel (2025)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2511.00079>.
